    "description": "CoreSite develops and operates interconnection-focused data centers in major U.S. metros. Its customers include enterprises, cloud platforms, network operators, and digital service providers that contract for colocation, power, and cross-connect capacity. The business is highly asset intensive because it is built around owned and leased data center facilities with recurring revenue from long-term customer contracts. Public disclosures describe a national platform of connected campuses and interconnection ecosystems within American Tower's U.S. data center business. American Tower acquired CoreSite in 2021, and Stonepeak entered the platform in 2022 through a minority investment that was later upsized to approximately 36%.",
